.TH GIT-SPARSE-CLONE 1
.SH NAME
git-sparse-clone \- sparse-clone selected directories from a large repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git sparse-clone
.I url
.RI [ paths... ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B git sparse-clone --append
.RI [ --dir
.IR dir ]
.I paths...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git sparse-clone
wraps Git sparse checkout (cone mode) to clone only selected directories from a
large repository, or to append directories to an existing sparse checkout.
.PP
When no paths are given, only top-level files are checked out (no
subdirectories), matching
.B git clone --sparse
defaults.
.PP
Paths are literal directory names. Glob patterns and negation
.RB ( ! path )
are not supported in this version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --dir " DIR"
Local target directory. Default: repository name derived from
.IR url .
With
.BR --append ,
an existing sparse repository (default: current repository).
.TP
.BI --branch " BRANCH"
Branch to clone. Default: remote default branch.
.TP
.BI --commit " SHA"
Check out a specific commit after clone.
.TP
.BI --depth " N"
Shallow clone depth. Default: 1. Use 0 for full history.
.TP
.B --no-filter
Disable
.B --filter=blob:none
(enabled by default).
.TP
.B --append
Add paths to an existing sparse checkout instead of cloning.
.TP
.BR --force ", " -f
Remove an existing target directory without prompting.
.TP
.BR --dry-run ", " -n
Print actions without changing anything.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git sparse-clone git@host:group/repo.git
git sparse-clone https://github.com/org/repo.git devtools scripts
git sparse-clone --dir my-sparse --branch main --depth 0 <url> src
git sparse-clone --append scripts config
git sparse-clone --append --dir /path/to/repo deploy
.fi
.SH NOTES
Requires Git 2.25 or newer.
